moth:
Though you hide them fast
From moth and from rust;
In your monstrous day

And laid them away in a box of gold;
Where long will cling the lips of the moth,
I have wrapped my dreams in a silken cloth;

motions:
And beauty-burning bodies manifest
Their warm, heart-melting motions to be wooed;
And passion boldly rising in my breast,

mote:
Became uncovered to my sight.
Some sound-mote in his passing tone
Caught in the meshes of my ear;

It levelled strong Euphrates in its course;
Supreme yet weightless as an idle mote
It seemed to tame the waters without force

mothah:
